<title>SWITZERLAND: Swissair Jan-Feb cargo traffic up 5.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Swissair Jan-Feb cargo traffic up 5.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swisscargo, the cargo arm of Swissair said January-February 1997 cargo traffic rose by 5.7 percent on the same period last year to 250.5 million freight tonne kilometres FTK.</p>
<p>The figures relate to cargo carried on Swissair code flights and do not include volumes carried on Sabena or other associates.</p>
<p>Swisscargo's January-February 1997 traffic, expressed in million FTK, with percentage change on January-February 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p> Traffic area	 Jan-Feb 97   Pct change</p>
<p>					   against Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>		  (in million FTK)</p>
<p> Europe		  10.1	  up     8.5pct</p>
<p> North America	 82.8	  down   5.9</p>
<p> South Atlantic	 7.8	  up    11.8</p>
<p> Middle East	    9.5	  down   6.8</p>
<p> Japan		   18.4	  up    13.9</p>
<p> Far East		63.7	  down   6.1</p>
<p> Africa		  23.7	  up     2.9</p>
<p> Total worldwide**  250.5	  up     5.7</p>
<p>Total includes cargo on passenger charters, special flights and freighter flights without a Swissair code.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
